{"resourceIdentifier":"3813","resourceName":"MOTOR VERDE FORESTRY CARBON PROJECT - GRANDAS DE SALIME (SPAIN)","description":"The Motor Verde Forestry Carbon Project – Grandas de Salime (Spain) consists in the reforestation of 86.94 ha in Grandas de Salime, Principality of Asturias, Spain. \r\nThe land over which reforestation is set to occur is part of the “Sierra de la Cuesta and Villarpedre” communal forest and is owned by the Grandas de Salime City Council. The area was affected by two wildfires in April and October 2017 that devastated the forest. Since then, no-human induced measures to restore the forest have been implemented. Furthermore, natural regeneration has been and continues to be impeded by the shrubland that now covers the area, thereby preventing natural regeneration.\r\nBeing an area with steep slopes and shallow soils, the land has been devoid of any forest vegetation since the fire and rainfall is now causing soil loss due to surface runoff. The hillside on which the works were carried out is located on the banks of the Salime Reservoir, which pours its waters directly into the Navia River.\r\nThe reforestation work consisted in extracting the burned material by using either the walking excavator felling head or a chainsaw. The burned material was then moved to the forest/logging trail and then a clearing was made using the felling head coupled to the walking excavator, whilst digging was underway. Then, the plots were treated, and seedlings planted by hand. A 10-metre wide strip adjacent to the clearing was made to serve as an auxiliary strip for fire-fighting purposes.\r\nThe project will remove a total amount of 50,370 tCO2 over a 100-year period, which works out at an average reduction of 504 tCO2 per year.\r\nThe project is part of Motor Verde initiative (see below). In Grandas de Salime, by means of recovering the forest that was lost in April and October 2017, the project will yield economic, social and environmental benefits. It will sequester carbon, it will restore ecosystems, and it will provide the local population with training and subsequent employment.","location":{"latitude":43.225135,"longitude":-6.828615},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-10-31","endExclusive":"2022-12-01","endInclusive":"2022-11-30"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3813"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Asturias"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1449"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Other Land Use"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_SUBCATERGORY_NAMES","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ARR"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AR-ACM0003"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_ACREAGE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"87 Hectares"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"AENOR CONFIA, S.A. (UNIPERSONAL)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"14/01/2025"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PERIOD_INFO","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1st, 09/01/2022 - 08/01/2072"}]}]}],"documentGroups":[{"code":"VCS_PIPELINE_DOCUMENTS","description":"VCS Pipeline Documents","documents":[{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=77018&IDKEY=niquwesdfmnk0iei23nnm435oiojnc909dsflk9809adlkmlkf8106207822","documentType":"Draft Project Description","documentName":"VCS_PROJ_DESC_PCP_3813_05OCT2022.pdf","uploadDate":"2022-10-25T18:50:47.387Z"},{"uri":"https://registry.verra.org/mymodule/ProjectDoc/Project_ViewFile.asp?FileID=76471&IDKEY=a903q4jsafkasjfu90amnmasdfkaidflnmdf9348r09dmfasdfl105453509","documentType":"Listin